From d6c5d5f2eb1e45bdfeb2f3e2d42af34810121d77 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Sun, 16 Aug 2026 15:34:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rebase kernel-session fixes onto latest main: SHA-NI,
 register aliases, GCC vector builtins by-value, FPU-flag toggles
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Semantic rebase after upstream absorbed the bulk of the prior session
(PR#77: \@ counter, relax ordering, realmode encodings, GOTPCREL,
directive guards). Every fix here is a VERIFIED remaining gap — each was
re-proven missing against 2bf26303 with a reproducer before re-landing,
and each output is byte-compared to GAS/GCC where applicable.

== Assembler ==
* SHA-NI: sha1rnds4 (0F 3A CC /r ib), sha1nexte/sha1msg1/sha1msg2
  (0F 38 C8..CA), sha256rnds2 (0F 38 CB, implicit %xmm0 — both the 2-op
  spelling and the explicit leading %xmm0 accepted), sha256msg1/2
  (0F 38 CC/CD). All NP encodings — no 0x66 prefix, unlike most
  0F38/0F3A SSE ops. Kernel lib/crypto/x86/sha{1,256}-ni-asm.S.
  PROOF: 9-instruction byte-diff vs GAS identical.
* Register aliases: the '=' spelling (NUM_BLKS = %rdx,
  sha256-avx2-asm.S), trailing comments on the definition line
  (CTX = %rdi # 1st arg glued the comment into the target),
  transitive chains (SRND = CTX; rotate_Xs' X_ = X0 permutation), and
  '=' definitions normalized to .set for the substitution pass.
  PROOF: alias.s byte-diff vs GAS identical.
* Stacked labels before macro invocations: ALTERNATIVE_2 emits
  '740: 740: \oldinstr' — stripping only one label left
  '740: RETPOLINE rax' unrecognized ('unhandled instruction:
  retpoline'). All leading label tokens are now peeled and re-emitted
  as separate statements. PROOF: stack.s byte-diff vs GAS identical.

== Driver / Preprocessor ==
* -mhard-float: clears the soft-float latch (kernel CC_FLAGS_FPU for
  kernel_fpu_begin() TUs; kbuild appends it after the kill flags —
  later-flag-wins is GCC semantics).
* -mno-sse now UNDEFINES __SSE__/__SSE2__/__SSE_MATH__/__SSE2_MATH__/
  __MMX_WITH_SSE__ (they are pre-defined for the common path; the early
  return left them visible and the NAP governor compiled its
  '#ifdef __SSE2__' vector code into a TU built with FPU_KILL_FLAGS).
  __MMX__ stays — GCC keeps it under -mno-sse (verified with -dM -E).

== Frontend / Lowering ==
* __builtin_ia32_maxps/minps (GCC vector-extension builtins; kernel
  code cannot include userspace intrin headers). New Vec128Value
  emission kind: raw builtins return the vector BY VALUE, unlike the
  _mm_* wrappers whose header dereferences the returned pointer. Two
  wrong-code bugs fixed on the way, both caught by the new runtime
  test BEFORE shipping: (1) returning the alloca pointer handed the
  caller a stack address instead of data; (2) the default I64 result
  type made the return path cqto-truncate lanes 2-3.
  PROOF: builtin_ia32_vector_value.c passes at -O0/-O2, matches GCC.
* mem2reg: span_at() guard — source_spans may be a PREFIX of the
  instruction list (several passes append instructions without spans);
  blind indexing panicked on sound/core/seq/seq_timer.c.

== Tests ==
* regression: builtin_ia32_vector_value.c (noinline ABI boundary +
  inline value flow + min/max lane routing).
* All prior session tests were already absorbed upstream and stay
  green (asm_macro_at_counter, asm_alt_skip_relax_order, ...).

VALIDATION: 685/685 lib, 185/185 regression, 50/50 correctness,
3/3 intrinsics, 86/86 linker, 300/300 differential fuzz vs GCC.
